          "Compare the source and the destination values before drawing a conclusion. Keep a version label on every file that can change. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Link each value to the field or page that supports it. The {topic} record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from underwriter instructions and party list.",
          "Keep a version label on every file that can change. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. A sample {topic} review checks CPL request, underwriter instructions, and the surviving value in the title production system."
