          "The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Check whether the definition changed during the period. Separate what was observed from what the team believes caused it. For {topic}, compare CPL request with the destination value rather than relying on a status label.",
          "Use case-level review to explain an outlier before calling it a trend. Report age and dependency, not only the total count. Include a routine case, a reopened case, and a cross-owner handoff. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. The {topic} close note cites the title production system, the approver, and the time of the final check."
